## TASK RUNNERS AND REPLS *bundles*

Two bundles extend this, and both are opt-in.

**`tools/task-runner`** adds a real task runner: `<C-w><C-r>` opens the task
list, and it is what gives `<Leader>rf` and `<Leader>rp` something to drive.
If those two keys do nothing on a fresh install, this is the bundle you are
missing.

**`tools/repl`** adds an interactive REPL beside the buffer, for languages
where you work by evaluating pieces rather than running the whole file.

    `<Leader>rs`   start the REPL
    `<Leader>rr`   restart it
    `<Leader>rh`   hide it
    `<Leader>rF`   focus it

**`terminal/better-term`** adds named terminals, so a long-running server
and a shell can both stay open and be reached by name.

Enable any of them from the bundle picker; see
[lesson six](@tutor:noethervim-06-bundles).

